\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{9}{2})=-1.352\\,127\\,380\\,…≈-1.352\\,127\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $-1.352\\,127$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-1.352\\,127\\,380\\,…+\\pi =1.789\\,465\\,272\\,…≈1.789\\,465 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.352\\,127\\,380\\,…+2\\pi =4.931\\,057\\,926\\,…≈4.931\\,058\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.789\\,466\\cdot 4.931\\,058≈8.824\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." 13194139538230 17592186576411 false] [17592186542157 1074 "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{9\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+9 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-9 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(-\\frac{9}{2}\\right)=-1.352\\,127\\,380\\,…≈-1.352\\,127\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $-1.352\\,127$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-1.352\\,127\\,380\\,…+\\pi =1.789\\,465\\,272\\,…≈1.789\\,465 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.352\\,127\\,380\\,…+2\\pi =4.931\\,057\\,