x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-\\theta }(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{{e}^{-\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\cancel{{e}^{-\\theta }}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{\\cancel{{e}^{-\\theta }}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4} \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4} & =0\\cdot (x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}) \\\\ y-\\frac{\\sqrt{