e:\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)+{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(ab)$ - the product rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})$ - the quotient rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡({c}^{m})=m{log}_{n}⁡(c)$ - the power rule\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{\\sqrt{z}})={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}{y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z})\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}{y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z})={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})+{log}_{3}⁡({y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z}).\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power rule for logarithms, we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})+{log}_{3}⁡({y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z})=2{log}_{3}⁡(x)+3{log}_{3}⁡(y)-\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{3}⁡(z).\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{\\sqrt{z}})=2{log}_{3}⁡(x)+3{log}_{3}⁡(y)-\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{3}⁡(z).\n$$" 13194139538230 17592186576411 false] [17592186543573 1074 "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)+{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(ab)$ - the product rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)$ - the quotient rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡({c}^{m})=m{log}_{n}⁡(c)$ - the power rule\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{\\sqrt{z}}\\right)={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}{y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z})\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}{y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z})={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})+{log}_{3}⁡({y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z}).\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power rule for logarithms, we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})+{log}_{3}⁡({y}^{3})-{log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{z})=2{log}_{3}⁡(x)+3{log}_{3}⁡(y)-\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{3}⁡(z).\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n{log}_{3}⁡\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{\\sqrt{z}}\\right)=2{log}_{3}⁡(x)+3{log}_{3}⁡(y)-\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{3}⁡(z).\n$$" 13194139538230 17592186576411 true] [17592186543576 1074 "The first three terms are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=\\frac{x}{4},\\,{a}_{2}=