sing the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-{X}^{5}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-{X}^{5}\\le y-1) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge (1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}((1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot {f}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot {f}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot 5{((1-y)^{1/5})}^{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538230 17592186576411 false] [17592186552417 1074 "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=1-{X}^{5}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/05/05534475aecc1d0ebad2234f1259d1b6fd1c6183e47ad763f17c87c5fdb06afb.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-{X}^{5}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-{X}^{5}\\le y-1) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge (1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute th